    <string name="tips_title">How to capture a panorama</string>
    <string name="tips_body">1. Tap Start\n2. Pan slowly — a frame fires when the marker reaches the center notch. The translucent ghost shows your previous frame: keep the new view overlapping about a third of it.\n3. Tap Done when you\'ve covered the scene\n\nRotate from your hips, keep the phone level. Pinch to zoom and tap to focus before starting — both lock during capture. Pan: ↕ for tall scenes; Undo removes a bad frame. Stitching continues even if you switch apps.</string>

